  "body": "### What is the issue with the File System Standard?\n\nI am playing with Chromes implementation (Chrome 136.0.7091.2 DEV, Windows 10).\n\nWhen there are a file and a directory with the same name, and one of them is removed, there is no way for me to know if the file or the directory has been removed. This is due to the absence of `changedHandle` in `FileSystemChangeRecord`s that are `disappeared`. Only the `changedHandle` can tell me if it's a file or a directory.\n\nI am not sure if this a problem in Chromes implementation, or a problem with the spec.",
